{
 "what": "ANIMATION [the town's activities] (rule 218(a), Paolo 10/26, LOCKED: 'everyone on your company... you can see them in the settlement, maybe flirting with a girl, maybe drinking some beer, maybe walking around, maybe talking to people... make it feel alive'). THE KEPT SOURCE OF EVERY TOWN ACTIVITY (rule 128): six things a man of his company does in a town, each a loop of held keys on the rig's man (the skeleton every person in the game is built on, so one list fits every look), with its own breaths and a few variants, so no two men do it in step. The pose ops, the axes and the bones are the idles' (records/target/animation/BOHEMIA_EVERYBODY_IDLES.json, read by the tool: a part named here that is not in this file's parts is the idles' part of that name). Walking the street is the walk every man already has (slices/rig_walk, RUN TWO's sheet: 'walk_plain'), steered by the player's wander (engine/bohemia_idles.js), its stops played as 'stall' or the bare idles.",
 "keys": "three a beat at 120; a pose is HELD (Crashbox stop-motion, rule 115(d)), never blended; a slot is two bars (24 keys) and starts and ends on the activity's REST pose, so any slot of an activity follows any other. AN ENVELOPE RAMPS SLOWER THAN THE GRID: a pose held ONE key sits between two different poses on the way (never a flicker out and back), the two sides of a turn never touch, and the gate measures every joint's travel between two drawn keys on the posed model itself (records/target/animation/towns/<look>/joints.json).",
